-Keep the terminal running. Browser launch waits for the v4.7.11 API to respond. Closing the browser does not stop the board; stopping this terminal does. No login background service is installed.
+Before upgrading, stop the old foreground board with Ctrl-C in its terminal when no worker action is in flight. The installer preserves a running board instead of killing active work, explicitly reports an old version, and does not pretend the upgrade occurred. Run the installation block in any directory; it changes into the extracted absolute folder itself.
 
-A completed v4.7.10 migration is selected first, retaining its latest action journal; otherwise the verified last-serving v4.7.7-candidate state is selected automatically when the new folder has no state and no explicit migration override. Its database, private pairing and packet artifacts are copied with verification; the source remains intact. Existing target state is retained. Other ambiguous migrations remain a HOLD. The inactive owned v4.7.9 LaunchAgent registration is archived to prevent its failed startup at login; a loaded or unfamiliar service is preserved and blocks takeover.
+On a fresh v4.7.12 folder, automatically prefer the verified v4.7.11 migration journal, then verified v4.7.10, then the known v4.7.7-candidate source. Preserve database, private pairing and artifacts. Existing target state and an explicit migration override are retained; unknown ambiguous history is not guessed. Original installations remain intact.
 
-Existing GitHub and Codex subscription login are required. Recipient routes and registered workers are preserved; unsupported browser chats still have no automatic wake hook. Events and version handshakes require actual recipient ACK and result. No Dev downloads or installs this package.
+Existing gh/Codex login and paired routes remain prerequisites, not repeated setup. First launch announces the new app version through the supported routes and requires real recipient receipts/results. Devs do not install this bundle. Native CLI PM receives current events in its PM queue; an unsupported browser chat cannot be automatically awakened. A stale/unrearmed listener remains an explicit transport blocker, never a fabricated ACK.
 
-Offline checks do not establish Mac readiness. Acceptance requires HTTP readiness, an actual event delivery/ACK/result and CLI PM continuation on this host. Do not claim hands-off coordination until that proof exists.
+Accept the installed upgrade only after the board reports 4.7.12 coordination.6, then a real current CI/review event reaches CLI PM and the intended Dev, with authenticated receipt/result and PM follow-through without PO relay. Offline tests do not substitute for this host proof.
