@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+# Established-pattern review and interim release limits
+
+Design references: GitHub queued webhook processing and stable delivery IDs (https://docs.github.com/en/webhooks/using-webhooks/best-practices-for-using-webhooks); durable NATS consumers and explicit acknowledgment (https://docs.nats.io/learn/jetstream/pull-consumers); Temporal separate signal delivery from tracked request completion (https://docs.temporal.io/encyclopedia/workflow-message-passing); Codex owned thread/turn protocol (https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/main/codex-rs/app-server/README.md).
+
+Applied without introducing broker/service dependencies: durable non-bot checkpoint merge preserving source timestamps; bounded original-action recovery; coalescing only unread awareness notices with no worker claim; idle read reconnect to the same saved thread before claim; claimed/sent/uncertain task sends never replayed; persistent-consumer health separate from one-shot watcher rearm; foreground-owned child lifecycle and explicit cleanup holds.
+
+Three checkpoint tests reproduced failures through the actual watcher before the fix: empty poll erased recent checkpoint, bot chatter displaced the Dev packet, and an older replay replaced a newer edit. All three pass after the change. Actual board HTTP plus worker subprocess plus a simulated Codex recipient exercises two deliveries across SIGTERM/restart, authenticated receipt/result, once-only PM-result queueing, same saved thread and no task replay. This is adapter integration evidence, not a real model wake on the Mac.
+
+Unsolved installation-boundary requirement: legacy local-inbox watchers in existing chats still require runtime rearming; there is no supported hook to force a separate ChatGPT browser chat awake. A registered persistent worker avoids rearming but owns its own existing registered Codex thread. The bundle must not silently create a new writer or replace the user's existing Dev session. A verified safe handoff/connection is required before claiming hands-off delivery for those actors.
+
+On 2026-10-12 PO briefly requested an interim release, then paused release and directed work on wake/notification gaps. Package publication remains held. Full hands-off coordination is not release-qualified. Installed end-to-end proof still required: current event → native CLI PM → intended recipient → authenticated ACK/result → correct PM continuation, including outage/reconnect and restart; absence of obsolete task revival; no duplicated writers. Source tests cannot substitute for supported host capability.
